{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Hark a journey to the Land of the Rising Sun a most wondrous quest I shall now weave for thee.\n\n**Day One: Arrival in Tokyo a City of Lights**\n\nFrom distant shores thou shalt arrive in Tokyo's grand embrace.\nNarita's gate shall yield thee to a bustling place.\nA swift train ride to Shinjuku's heights\nWhere towering structures greet the day's first lights.\nA hotel's chamber a haven sweet\nTo rest thy weary limbs and weary feet.\nThen wander forth through Shinjuku Gyoen's grace\nA tranquil garden a most lovely space.\nDinner awaits a culinary delight\nRamen's warmth to banish fading light.\n\n**Day Two: Tokyo's Temples and Traditions**\n\nTo Asakusa's temple we shall now proceed\nSenso-ji's grandeur a pious deed.\nLanterns glow with stories old and deep\nWhile merchants chant their wares while mortals sleep.\nThen to the Imperial Palace a sight to behold\nWhere history's echoes bravely unfold.\nGinza's streets a shopper's paradise\nLuxury and elegance before thine eyes.\nA Sumida River cruise a gentle flow\nReflecting Tokyo's vibrant glow.\n\n**Day Three: Hakone's Mountain Majesty**\n\nA journey forth to Hakone's verdant scene\nWhere mountains rise majestic serene.\nLake Ashi's waters a mirror bright\nReflecting peaks in morning light.\nA cruise upon the lake a peaceful sound\nAs nature's beauty doth abound.\nThe Hakone Open-Air Museum a wondrous art\nSculptures and landscapes set apart.\nVolcanic hot springs a soothing balm\nTo ease thy cares and keep thee calm.\n\n**Day Four: Kyoto's Ancient Charm**\n\nUpon the Shinkansen a swift train ride\nTo Kyoto's heart where history doth reside.\nFushimi Inari's gates a vermillion dream\nThousands of torii a vibrant gleam.\nKiyomizu-dera Temple a wooden stage\nOverlooking Kyoto's turning age.\nGion's district a geisha's grace\nA fleeting glimpse a mystical space.\nA traditional tea ceremony a ritual fine\nA moment's peace a truly divine sign.\n\n**Day Five: Kyoto's Golden Pavilion and Gardens**\n\nKinkaku-ji's splendor a golden hue\nReflecting in the pond a wondrous view.\nRyoan-ji's garden a Zen delight\nFifteen stones arranged in shadowed light.\nArashiyama Bamboo Grove a verdant maze\nWhere sunlight filters in a hazy daze.\nTenryu-ji Temple's gardens serene\nA peaceful haven a tranquil scene.\nNishiki Market's bounty a feast for the eyes\nLocal delicacies a delightful prize.\n\n**Day Six: Nara's Deer and Todai-ji's Might**\n\nTo Nara we journey where deer roam free\nA sacred park for all to see.\nTodai-ji Temple houses a giant Buddha's form\nA testament to faith weathering every storm.\nKasuga Taisha Shrine lanterns glow\nA pathway to spirits soft and low.\nReturn to Kyoto for a final night\nTo savor memories bathed in golden light.\n\n**Day Seven: Farewell Japan**\n\nWith heavy heart we bid farewell\nTo Japan's beauty a wondrous spell.\nFrom Kansai Airport thy flight will soar\nBearing memories forevermore.\nMay thy journey be filled with joy and grace\nAnd Japan's spirit light thy face.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.011765611357986927}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.5393308401107788}, {"token": "▁journey", "logprob": -0.9428325891494751}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.0012685356196016073}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.06821470707654953}, {"token": "▁Land", "logprob": -0.23844066262245178}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.041723914444446564}, {"token": "▁Rising", "logprob": -4.172316494077677e-06}, {"token": "▁Sun", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.03884647414088249}, {"token": "▁most", "logprob": -0.0921824648976326}, {"token": "▁wondrous", "logprob": -0.03875691443681717}, {"token": "▁quest", "logprob": -0.21989865601062775}, {"token": "▁I", "logprob": -0.18333247303962708}, {"token": "▁shall", "logprob": -0.007961917668581009}, {"token": 